From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:24:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: drop shadows, and redirect visuals.

Opening a recovered document, Word's AirSpace asks for a DropShadow and
then for a RedirectVisual, and asserted on each.

A drop shadow is as Windows makes one: a blur radius of 9, opaque black,
full opacity, no offset, no mask, and nothing it is set to refused; its
blur radius, color, offset and opacity are animatable.  It is drawn
under what its sprite draws, moved by its offset; with no blur in
Direct2D here, the softening is a few rectangles, each larger and
fainter than the last.

A redirect visual is a container visual that draws its source again.
As measured on Windows through PrintWindow, the source is drawn at the
redirect visual's own origin, its own offset not counting, and still
where it is itself; any visual may be the source, one the redirect
visual is in included, so the drawing again stops a few levels deep.

The tests of both pass on Windows as here; the redirect's pixels, read
from the screen here, are Windows'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 20248843485d22d93cd02c3ea5f757abce2341b2)

